; The ONE variable: `layout_direction = 3` on a FoldableContainer. RTL moves
; three things at once in the SAME node, and Godot moves them together: the
; fold arrow goes to the trailing edge and, while folded, becomes
; `folded_arrow_mirrored` (foldable_container.cpp:293-300,428-435); the title
; text starts at the style's leading margin with `title_alignment` LEFT and
; RIGHT swapped (`:503-511`); and the content is inset from the panel style's
; RIGHT margin (`:365-367`). The folded pair shows the arrow and the alignment
; swap, the unfolded pair the content inset, each against its own LTR twin.
; unit-foldable-container.tscn moves folded/alignment/position at direction
; LTR, so none of this is visible there. The folded pair carries no children:
; a folded container's children are hidden by Godot at sort time, which this
; previewer cannot yet reproduce, and a child here would put that separate
; divergence into this fixture's picture.

